  "commits_data": [
    {
      "id": "2acd5c706e46151a0534cf12e94670bb969aecca",
      "short_id": "2acd5c70",
      "created_at": "2020-12-02T13:32:50.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "5798b91c1526747bf688b6746b33562c1b24a9e0"
      ],
      "title": "packet-tls-utils:Move ssl_sha_init() and ssl_md5_init() out of a loop",
      "message": "packet-tls-utils:Move ssl_sha_init() and ssl_md5_init() out of a loop\n\nInstead of calling ssl_sha_init() and ssl_sha_cleanup() in\na loop, call the newly-created ssl_sha_reset(), to avoid\ncreating and releasing contexts.\nAlso, do the same for ssl_md5_init() and ssl_md5_cleanup().\n\nBesides the performance improvement,\nthis should also fix Coverity 1450156 and 1450693,\nwhich detect the multiple calls to ssl_sha_cleanup()\nand ssl_md5_cleanup() as a double-free.\n",
      "author_name": "Moshe Kaplan",
      "author_email": "me@moshekaplan.com",
